From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hollitizz <valentin.caure@epitech.eu>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:27:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ios: an Apple TV app of a game (DM_TVOS=1)

build_ipa.sh with DM_TVOS=1 builds the game as a tvOS app, unsigned IPA or prepared Xcode project:
project_tv.yml, the frameworks the appletvos SDK has (gen_build.py DM_SDK), a layered icon and Top
Shelf images made from the game's icon (tools/tv_icon.swift), stage_resources.sh accepting
appletvos. The shader libraries stay the iOS ones, which tvOS loads, so the shader chain is the same.
On tvOS:
- the game files, saves and logs live in Library/Caches (main.m): tvOS apps cannot write Documents;
- a controller's presses reach the game only (DmRootVC is a GCEventViewController), and a Back press
  stays in the game instead of leaving for the Home screen; UIKit gets the controller while a user
  or keyboard alert is up;
- the saves are copied into the app's preferences a few seconds after each save, as the cloud-save
  path does (SourcesTV/TVSaves.m, LZFSE), and come back when the system purged Library/Caches;
  a store past 900 KB goes to Library/Preferences/tv-saves;
- there is no settings screen and no in-game menu (SourcesTV/TVFront.m).
The save goes out when the app resigns active, not only in the background: a swipe in the app
switcher ends it with no background step. Ported from TVPort.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Apple TV builds of a game (DM_TVOS=1), ported from TVPort: a fork product choice
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#85

